      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not give aspirin to a 6-year-old child because it can cause Reye's syndrome, a rare but serious condition. Instead, administer a dose of acetaminophen (Tylenol) or ibuprofen (Motrin/Advil), following the specific weight-based dosing instructions on the label. Always consult your pediatrician for medical advice if the fever is very high, persists, or if he appears lethargic.",
